        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 78-year-old male patient, admitted on 13/02/2025 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed reduced air entry bilaterally, prolonged expiratory phase, and accessory muscle use. Oxygen saturation was diminished at rest. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure with mild hypercapnia. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia or pneumothorax. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and closely monitored vital signs. He responded well to treatment with clear clinical improvement. He is discharged home in stable condition. Please continue maintenance bronchodilator therapy and ensure regular COPD follow-up. Do not hesitate to contact me if needed.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
